## 3. Current Production Status

### 3.1 Live Deployment (Verified 2026-10-19 21:15 Africa/Cairo)

**Infrastructure:**
- All 6 PM2 services online
- WhatsApp authenticated and delivering
- Message mode: LIVE (database setting)
- Test pipeline: Thenile14 full scan completed (~2 min)
- Notification delivery: 17 sent successfully

**Network Access:**
- Local: http://127.0.0.1:3000
- LAN: http://192.168.1.111:3000 (Wi-Fi, Private profile)
- Remote: http://26.182.57.137:3000 (Radmin VPN)

**Performance Metrics:**
- Account scan: ~2 minutes per account (26 accounts × 2 min = 52 min full cycle)
- Event dispatcher: 10-second polling interval
- Assistant monitoring: 30-second cycle
- PDF scanner: 5-minute schedule

### 3.2 Known Issues & Technical Debt

**High Priority:**
1. **Mistral API Rate Limits**: Both keys exhausted, need more keys or smarter usage
2. **No User Channels**: Only control number receives notifications (0 user_channels records)
3. **WhatsApp Instability**: Frequent reconnects seen in logs
4. **Sequential Account Processing**: 52-minute full cycle blocks new scans
5. **No Graceful Shutdown**: PM2 restart loses in-flight scans

**Medium Priority:**
6. **No Structured Logging**: Console.log everywhere, hard to debug production
7. **No Metrics/Telemetry**: No Prometheus/Grafana, blind to performance
8. **Hardcoded Timeouts**: Magic numbers (10s, 30s, 2min) not configurable
9. **No Health Checks**: PM2 restarts but no liveness/readiness probes
10. **PDF OCR Quality**: Poor Arabic text extraction from scanned documents

**Low Priority:**
11. **No TypeScript**: Pure JavaScript, no type safety
12. **Test Coverage**: 40/41 tests pass (97.6%), but only unit tests, no integration tests
13. **No CI/CD**: Manual deployment, no GitHub Actions
14. **Dark Mode Incomplete**: Some UI components still hardcoded colors
15. **No Documentation**: README outdated, no API docs

### 3.3 Security Audit Findings

**Credentials:**
- DPAPI encryption for Gmail/Telegram at rest
- WhatsApp session in .wwebjs_auth/ (plain Chromium profile)
- Mistral keys in .env (plain text)
- MCP bearer token in .env (plain text)

**Network:**
- Firewall rule restricts TCP 3000 to Private profile
- MCP server bound to 127.0.0.1:3101
- No HTTPS (HTTP only on localhost)
- No authentication on dashboard (read-only mode excuse)

**Code:**
- SQL prepared statements used, but no parameterization in dynamic queries
- No input validation on portal scraper (trusts ETA portal HTML structure)
- Path traversal risk in PDF scanner (resolved path check present)
- No rate limiting on API endpoints

